    <p style="font-size: 12pt;">4.</p>
    <h3 style="font-weight: bold;">U. T. Pan American: Request for approval of authorization and changes related to a sports recreation and wellness facility fee; incidental and other fees; and course-related incidental fees effective Fall 2007</h3>
    
    <h4 style="text-align: center; margin-top: 30px;">RECOMMENDATION</h4>
    
    <p>The Chancellor concurs in the recommendation of the Executive Vice Chancellor for Academic Affairs, the Vice Chancellor and General Counsel, and President Cárdenas that the following authorizations and changes related to special, incidental, and course fees at U. T. Pan American for Fall 2007 be approved:</p>
    
    <ol>
        <li>
            <p>a. A Sports Recreation and Wellness Facility Fee of <span data-field="fee_amount_1">{{ fee_amount_1 }}</span> per student per semester for the sports recreation and wellness facility scheduled to open in <span data-field="semester_1">{{ semester_1 }}</span>;</p>
        </li>
        <li>
            <p>b. Charge of the Alternative Certification Program (ACP)/Alternative Certification Program Extension Fee either directly to the students participating in the ACP or to the school district employing ACP students, at the discretion of the ACP director;</p>
        </li>
        <li>
            <p>c. A Graduate Program Fee of <span data-field="fee_amount_2">{{ fee_amount_2 }}</span> per semester for students in the graduate Clinical Psychology or Experimental Psychology programs;</p>
        </li>
        <li>
            <p>d. Course-Related Fees ranging from <span data-field="fee_range_1">{{ fee_range_1 }}</span> to <span data-field="fee_range_2">{{ fee_range_2 }}</span>, as attached on Pages 9 - 13; and</p>
        </li>
        <li>
            <p>e. Rename the approved Computer Access Fee as the Information Technology Access Fee.</p>
        </li>
    </ol>

    <h4 style="text-align: center; margin-top: 30px;">BACKGROUND INFORMATION</h4>
    
    <p>The new special fee for the sports, recreation and wellness facility was approved by students in a referendum held March 29 - April 1, 2004, authorized by the 79th Texas Legislature in 2005, and codified in Section 54.5421 of the Texas Education Code.</p>
    
    <p>U. T. Pan American currently bills the ACP fees to the school districts that employ ACP students and the school district then collects the charges from the students via a payroll deduction. U. T. Pan American requests approval to have the option to charge the fee directly to students entering at school districts that do not or cannot recoup program costs. The fee is used to defray the cost of administering the ACP, including on-site internship supervision, evaluation and travel costs, seminars and mentoring. This fee is consistent with applicable statutory requirements under Sections 54.504 and 55.16 of the Texas Education Code.</p>
</div>

<div class="page">
    <p style="font-size: 12pt;">The proposed new Graduate Program Fee would be used to defray the cost associated with the maintenance of administering standard practices, professional level psychological tests, and the associated scoring and interpretive software, as well as to purchase instructional materials. This fee is consistent with applicable statutory requirements under Sections 54.504 and 55.16 of the Texas Education Code.</p>
    
    <p>Proposed new course-related fees would be used to defray specific costs associated with offering various courses in communications and the arts. These fees are consistent with applicable statutory requirements for incidental fees under Section 54.504 of the Texas Education Code.</p>
    
    <p>The current Computer Access Fee is used to defray administrative costs incurred in providing access to and supervision of computer labs. Changing the name to the Information Technology Access Fee and the fee description will allow the fee to defray costs incurred in students' use of information technology including the provision of access and supervision of computer labs, supplying network access and infrastructure, servers and other information technology-related hardware, software, and services. This fee is consistent with applicable statutory requirements under Sections 54.504 and 55.16 of the Texas Education Code.</p>
</div>

