    <p style="font-size: 12pt;">5.</p>
    <h3 style="font-weight: bold;">U. T. Permian Basin: Request for approval of laboratory and course-related incidental fees effective Fall 2007</h3>
    
    <h4 style="text-align: center; margin-top: 30px;">RECOMMENDATION</h4>
    
    <p>The Chancellor concurs in the recommendation of the Executive Vice Chancellor for Academic Affairs, the Vice Chancellor and General Counsel, and President Watts that the following laboratory and course-related incidental fees at U. T. Permian Basin effective Fall 2007 be approved:</p>
    
    <ol>
        <li>
            <p>a. New Laboratory Fees ranging from <span data-field="fee_range_3">{{ fee_range_3 }}</span> to <span data-field="fee_range_4">{{ fee_range_4 }}</span> per course to cover the actual cost of materials and supplies used by students enrolled in laboratory courses; and</p>
        </li>
        <li>
            <p>b. Course-Related Fees ranging from <span data-field="fee_range_5">{{ fee_range_5 }}</span> to <span data-field="fee_range_6">{{ fee_range_6 }}</span>, as attached on Pages 15 - 17.</p>
        </li>
    </ol>

    <h4 style="text-align: center; margin-top: 30px;">BACKGROUND INFORMATION</h4>
    
    <p>The proposed new laboratory fees are within the range authorized by law and are consistent with the statutory requirements under Section 54.501(a) of the Texas Education Code.</p>
    
    <p>The proposed new course-related fees would be used to defray specific costs associated with offering various courses. These fees are consistent with applicable statutory requirements for incidental fees under Section 54.504 of the Texas Education Code.</p>
</div>

